      3 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَاعَرَتْ حَالِبَهَا</span></b> , [inf. n., app., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِعَارٌ</span>, q. v.,] said
of a ewe or she-goat, (K,) and of a she-camel,
(TA,) <i>She befouled her milker with her dung.</i>
(TA voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِعَارٌ</span>.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَاعَرَتْ إِلَى حَالِبِهَا</span> <i>She</i> (a ewe
or goat, and a camel,) <i>hastened to her milker.</i>
(TA.)

